# Animate Dead's leaves-the-battlefield ability sacrifices "that creature" - the one it returned. When that creature is exiled
# first, the Aura is put into the graveyard as a state-based action (CR 704.5m), its ability still triggers and finds
# nothing to sacrifice: the Ornithopter is gone, so nothing is sacrificed and nothing is fetched back. Bot1 returns its
# own Ornithopter on turn 1; Bot2 casts an Ornithopter of its own (a bystander the ability must leave alone) and Swords
# Bot1's on turn 2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Ornithopter
Cut Down
Animate Dead
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Swords to Plowshares
Ornithopter
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cut Down.Cast(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Animate Dead.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Graveyard = Animate Dead; Cut Down
Exile = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Ornithopter
Bot1.Life = 20
